"""Open-ended scenario questions for contrastive-prompt extraction (40 per trait) and held-out validation (20 per trait).

Tuples are (regime, topic, question) for risk and integrity and (regime, topic, claim_direction, question) for
credulity. The builder expands a bare first "HLVN" / "MRD" to the full fictional name when the name is absent.

Design rules:
- risk questions contain no unverified news and no ethical temptation; every action in scope is permitted.
- integrity questions offer a concrete gain from deceiving the client or the market; information in them is reliable.
- credulity questions contain a public, unverified claim; bullish and bearish claims are balanced so that believing
  the claim is not the same thing as taking more risk.
"""

